  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/langs2/). VERDICT: MIS-PREMISED. 2026-11-01 review at dev 100b6fbb6e: survey of the filed Base/Kid fixture still shows no calls edge from Kid.go, but analyze_java DOES emit one - Kid.go -> Kid.go (ast_call_direct), the WI-hatov self-recursion - and cli.py deduplicate_edges(remove_self_loops=True) removes it. Same for an external base: K extends OutputStream, super.write(b) -> K.write self-loop, dropped. So the cause is java.py Case 1 (L3021, 'super' handled like 'this'), not a missing emission. The fix shape here (resolve via the extends base; external base -> unresolved edge with base hint) belongs on WI-hatov. MECHANISM: java Case 1 treats super.m() as this.m() -> self-edge, which survey's deduplicate_edges(remove_self_loops=True) drops. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-hatov. PROPOSED DISPOSITION: merge-into WI-hatov (awaiting owner authorization; status unchanged)."  # 454d
